---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/postscript-vs-brevo';
const title = "Postscript vs Brevo for Shopify: 2026 Comparison";
const desc = "Choose the Shopify integration before comparing channels A Shopify workflow and migration comparison, with current supplier sources.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is the old Brevo Shopify integration the current option?",
    "answer": "Brevo\u2019s current guide directs Shopify merchants to Brevo PushOwl and describes replacement of the previous integration. Check your installed app and account before following older instructions."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Brevo guarantee GDPR compliance?",
    "answer": "No vendor choice establishes your compliance. Review the actual data processing terms, capture records, purposes and destination-market requirements."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I replace Postscript to consolidate billing?",
    "answer": "Only after the intended text workflows, eligibility and total costs are checked in the actual proposed product. Invoice count alone is insufficient."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
      <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Postscript vs Brevo for Shopify</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl">Choose the Shopify integration before comparing channels</p></header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Identify which Brevo product is being quoted</h2>
        <p>Brevo’s <a href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360014912879-Brevo-PushOwl-app-for-Shopify-Connect-your-Shopify-store-with-Brevo-PushOwl">current Shopify guide</a> describes Brevo PushOwl, combining email, SMS, web push and WhatsApp. It says this replaces the previous Brevo Shopify integration. An older Brevo account or API workflow should not be treated as identical to a new PushOwl installation.</p>
        <h2>Start with an integration inventory</h2>
        <p>Record the installed Shopify app, account owner, connected shop, automation engine and billing account. List custom API calls and transactional templates separately. Ask support which records and settings carry into the intended product. This makes the comparison concrete: migrating an existing Brevo setup is a different project from adding Postscript to a working email stack.</p>
        <h2>Map channel permissions individually</h2>
        <p>An email address, phone number and browser subscription represent different reachable audiences. For a proposed multichannel welcome journey, record eligibility per channel and what happens when only one permission is present. Do not infer SMS permission from email signup, or permission to contact a person on WhatsApp from the existence of a phone number.</p>
        <h2>Use geography as an eligibility check</h2>
        <p>Build a list of actual destination markets and required sender types, then request written coverage and registration requirements for each channel. A vendor’s location does not establish legal suitability, residency guarantees or immunity from complaints. Do not turn US-versus-EU labels into a platform ranking; confirm contractual data terms and the specific sending program.</p>
        <h2>Reconcile marketing and transactional ownership</h2>
        <p>Before moving order confirmations or password-related messages, identify the actual sending service and its authentication, limits and failure alerts. A Shopify marketing app comparison does not establish transactional API equivalence. Keep the existing operational route until its replacement has been independently checked; promotions and essential account messages need different failure handling.</p>
        <h2>Proposed cart and repeat-purchase checks</h2>
        <p>For cart recovery, inspect entry on the intended Shopify event, purchase exit and the behavior of queued email/text messages when a customer opts out. For repeat purchase, test a refunded order and a subscription renewal before making eligibility depend on order totals. These are proposed validation cases, not observed results or promises that every channel shares one suppression tree.</p>
        <h2>Cost consolidation using the right account</h2>
        <p>Get the relevant PushOwl or Brevo quote and a Postscript quote for the same intended work. Separate email volume, reachable profiles, text usage by country, other channels, support and migration labor. Establish which balance or allowance each automation consumes, including peak operational traffic. Do not reuse a legacy Brevo price or assume one combined bill reduces total cost.</p>
        <h2>Decide between consolidation and a split stack</h2>
        <p>Evaluate Brevo PushOwl when its demonstrated Shopify multichannel workflows match the intended replacement. Evaluate Postscript when the project is a dedicated Shopify text program alongside an email sender you plan to keep. A split by country or channel is justified only when eligibility, ownership and suppression transfer are documented; geography alone is not an architecture.</p>
        <h2>Postscript scope and evidence limits</h2>
        <p>Postscript describes <a href="https://postscript.io/features">Shopify SMS workflows</a> and has announced <a href="https://postscript.io/email">Postscript Email with a waitlist</a>. Confirm account access before retiring an email sender. Supplier descriptions checked November 25, 2026; no live account tests, performance results or compliance ranking are claimed here.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/brevo-vs-mailchimp">Brevo vs Mailchimp</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/brevo-vs-omnisend">Brevo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-mailchimp">Postscript vs Mailchimp</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/beauty">Email apps for beauty stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Postscript vs Brevo FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
